# cargo-fuzz's outputs, which the README names but nothing enforced until now:
# `seeds/` and `fuzz_targets/` are the sources and are committed, while the
# corpus that accumulates, the inputs that crashed, and the build target are
# not. The `crash-*` family is what libFuzzer writes next to the crate when it
# is run from `fuzz/` instead of through `cargo fuzz tmin`.
/corpus
/artifacts
/target
/crash-*
/oom-*
/leak-*
/timeout-*
/slow-unit-*
